<%#
  A rendered markdown document, or the reason there isn't one.

  `body` arrives already rendered, as a SafeBuffer: `renderMarkdown` lives in
  `app/helpers`, which is inert in the vendored trails — a controller's
  `_helpers` never reaches the view's scope chain (see shared/_status-badge
  for the same note and the upstream fix). The controller therefore renders
  and the view places, which is also why the escaping decision is made once,
  in the helper, over untrusted agent-authored prose.

  The read error is shown rather than swallowed: a story whose file has been
  renamed or rehomed is exactly when someone opens its page, and "no document"
  and "could not read the document" are different answers. Matches ringo's
  `MarkdownErr` block.
%>
<% if (error !== "") { %>
  <p class="note">Could not read the document: <%= error %></p>
<% } else if (body !== null) { %>
  <article class="markdown"><%= body %></article>
<% } else { %>
  <p class="muted">No document.</p>
<% } %>
